AI usage guidelines:
Since Ai seems to be unescapable in this day and age especially online, i figured a rule about Ai code should be put in place for now.
Fully using Ai to generate any part of the Code you commit is banned and will not be merged, same goes for the text in your PR or in your Issue report.
Using Ai as a tool to assist you the MAIN writer of code in some super small areas, like for example the google search ai thingy after searching up an issue is allowed tho (if you really need it)
And i mean, why wouldnt you want to code yourself but let the bots do it for you, thats a little lame if you ask me.

Any usage of AI has to be marked when submitting a Pull request and an explanation has to be given. 
If im unsure in some parts i will just ask you a couple questions to check.
Thanks for understanding :)

And for everyone else:

All Contributions are welcome, if that is help on the Weblate, help with an issue the app is facing or a pull reqest with a new feature, it truely all is appreceated.
Thank you everybode for helping so much with the contributions, especially since i still have school and dont got a whole lot of time for Coding per day.
Thanks thannks thanks :)

- Elektron
